One encoder for every connection that sends a shared screen at one size, in the
Objective-C SDK, as the C++ wrapper does (patches/wrapper/0017): the encoder factory the
plugin passes is wrapped in //libwebrtc's SharedEncoderFactory (both initializers that
take an RTCVideoEncoderFactory), ObjCVideoTrackSource tags the frames of a source marked
with RTCVideoSource's enableFogataSharedEncode, and the field trial
Fogata-SharedScreenEncode/Enabled/ turns it on. Without the trial, or for a source not
marked (cameras), nothing changes.

